<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:06Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Berlin's punitive measures unlikely to deter Putin: experts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6686f7b76ee7a7f5c69a6b07e5fab50e0dca3f9968534eff13388e7fc2deaec5</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-punitive-measures-unlikely-to-deter-putin-experts/a-78803217--e7ac43c2d794.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-punitive-measures-unlikely-to-deter-putin-experts/a-78803217?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced punitive measures after publicly blaming Russia for an attempted airport drone attack. But a former diplomat, political and security analysts warn it will likely do little to deter the Kremlin.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6937b5a552e0b796ac45ff61a6a5619c53c5b4aa665ea1e25cfd3daa8faf5394</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--91d3b884dfe8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3791a648bdf0cf1eadb611f5cbd887923b5c0a1e98607fe3585e107bbf60641c</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--b38376dc9663.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ef5c69ec2e24fb5b0da414bbfe02c0fad7b27babb0284b2a319281861714b35</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--a133d5f50599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Explosive devices found near power plant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfacc3dd92ab34a8698bbd295f0a3b5d6e836288fc999012592a191c24c9bb6b</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741--1f323d2ba311.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-explosive-devices-found-near-power-plant/live-78583741?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police say they found unconventional explosive and incendiary devices near the Jänschwalde power plant in Brandenburg. Meanwhile, Germany's top diplomat says Algeria could become an important supplier of gas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: How to woo voters with an immigrant background</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbef672fc710766de080d982badc1e0c242ecfc0fad65ae2c3f2312ef4e8af13</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775--5e7baf534d71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of voters in Germany with an immigrant background is rising. Yet the established parties barely manage to reach them. Why not?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's hybrid attacks on Germany: When is it 'war?'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b461f4b8bffea5592d9b16cdbf122e718f1fa93ebecdab5f22622310f7fae5c1</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-hybrid-attacks-on-germany-when-is-it-war/a-78784262--c21b1b4967ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-hybrid-attacks-on-germany-when-is-it-war/a-78784262?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German government is holding Russia responsible for an unsuccessful attack in Leipzig. Yet many feel that its response has been too mild.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football: Anyomi, London City and the German exodus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0f27001550d80ea3dbefc371fc6edb4be1ccb368057dba925f12d2a69b83e0a</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131--88cc548694ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nicole Anyomi has joined Alexia Putellas and other star names in signing for the ambitious English club London City Lionesses. The Germany winger told DW England is a better place to develop her game than back home.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--d7968a32f7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c2db82dae4a4580ce0ad6671f3326ef7b9f59bff909dbcfa0c52487272de87</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--3ab5f0359b92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ea5c43f16912fc8d07b404b180c35c27c0bd22aca18731970cfbc678a785db0</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--c7c332adab8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
